{"event_type": "attempt_started", "mode": "agent_tools", "run_id": "llama31_8b_q4__agent_tools__T05__rep03", "system_prompt": "You are solving a controlled benchmark task.\nYou may only use the available tools.\nDo not assume internet access.\nDo not access files outside the workspace.\nDo not invent unavailable data.\nProduce the required output files.\nWhen finished, call submit.\n\nProtocol rules:\n- Reply with exactly one <tool_call> block per turn.\n- Do not write prose, markdown, or code outside the <tool_call> block.\n- The JSON inside <tool_call> must be one object with exactly two top-level fields: \"tool\" and \"args\".\n- The \"tool\" field must be a string: \"read\", \"write\", \"edit\", \"bash\", or \"submit\".\n- The \"args\" field must be an object.\n- Tool results can be long. Do not copy tool-result content into your reply; choose the next tool call.\n- For multi-line Python, use write to create a script, then bash to run it; avoid giant inline bash commands.\n\nAvailable tools and argument schemas:\n- read: {\"path\": \"relative/path.txt\"} or {\"path\": \"relative/path.txt\", \"max_chars\": 12000}\n- write: {\"path\": \"relative/path.txt\", \"content\": \"complete file content\"}\n- edit: {\"path\": \"relative/path.txt\", \"old\": \"text to replace\", \"new\": \"replacement text\", \"replace_all\": true}\n- bash: {\"command\": \"python src/solution.py\"}\n- submit: {\"message\": \"done\"}\n\nValid examples:\n<tool_call>\n{\"tool\": \"read\", \"args\": {\"path\": \"inputs/example.csv\"}}\n</tool_call>\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"tool\": \"write\", \"args\": {\"path\": \"outputs/example.txt\", \"content\": \"complete file content\"}}\n</tool_call>\n\nInvalid examples:\n- {\"tool\": {\"args\": {\"path\": \"inputs/example.csv\"}}}\n- {\"read\": {\"path\": \"inputs/example.csv\"}}\n- prose before or after the <tool_call> block\n- copying a CSV or script into the response without using the write tool\n\nUse this exact shape for every response:\n<tool_call>\n{\"tool\": \"...\", \"args\": {...}}\n</tool_call>", "task_id": "T05", "task_prompt": "Task ID: T05\nTitle: Clean GTFS coordinates and times\nFamily: gtfs_processing\n\nRemove stops whose latitude or longitude is outside the valid range, remove duplicate stop rows keeping the first occurrence, replace blank stop names with a non-empty placeholder, and preserve valid extended GTFS times.\n\nAvailable input files:\n- inputs/gtfs/sample_city_gtfs.zip\n\nRequired output files:\n- outputs/t05_gtfs_cleaning_report.json\n- outputs/t05_clean_stops.csv\n- outputs/t05_clean_stop_times.csv\n\nOutput requirements:\n- outputs/t05_gtfs_cleaning_report.json:\n  - JSON object with integer fields: invalid_coordinates_removed, duplicate_stops_removed, missing_stop_names_filled, n_clean_stops, n_clean_stop_times.\n- outputs/t05_clean_stops.csv:\n  - CSV columns: stop_id, stop_name, stop_lat, stop_lon\n- outputs/t05_clean_stop_times.csv:\n  - CSV columns: trip_id, arrival_time, departure_time, stop_id, stop_sequence\n  - Include exactly the stop_times rows whose stop_id remains in outputs/t05_clean_stops.csv.\n  - Preserve valid GTFS times beyond 24:00:00.\n- Every CSV output must be RFC 4180 compliant: quote any field that contains a comma, a double quote, or a newline, so that each row has exactly as many fields as the header.\n", "timestamp": "2026-10-30T22:56:33.609048+00:00"}
